    "details": {
      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><strong>Inspector Corvin Tallis</strong> is one of the Exchange's few breathing staff: a tall, thin man in his fifties in a grey uniform coat, a brass measuring chain at his belt and a small black book of door openings in his hand. Polite, precise and slightly too close, he asks questions that each have exactly one answer.</p><p><strong>GM notes (Part 7).</strong> Pressure, not a villain: he has counted forty-one openings of a door recorded as sealed and will post a notice at noon. Delay: Persuasion DC 15 (advantage with the audit); permit: DC 17 with the audit; lie: Deception DC 16 (notice still posts). Nan can make him late. Never violence.</p>",
        "public": ""
      },
