      "name": "GM Reference: Corvin Tallis, Voice and Rounds",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Inspector Corvin Tallis, Inspector of Thresholds</h2><p><em>\"Is the door sealed? The ledger says it is. My book says it opens. One of these is wrong.\"</em></p><p><strong>Body:</strong> one of the few breathing staff: a tall, thin, living human in his fifties, grey uniform coat, a brass measuring chain looped at his belt. Writes in a small black book of door openings.</p><p><strong>Job:</strong> inspects thresholds: that every door does what the ledger says it does. Posts notices of irregularity on the public boards. <strong>Not a villain, not hostile</strong>: pressure. He and Sabeline want the same thing, for opposite reasons.</p><p><strong>Quill:</strong> has hired Quill twice to repair doors and respects the work; has started to wonder why Quill's repairs are so good on doors that are \"sealed\".</p><p><strong>Rounds:</strong> rides the <strong>tenth-hour trolley</strong> every night now and times it with his watch (Nan finds this rude). Appears in Scene 5 (night custody office) and possibly at the cold door in Scene 7.</p><p><strong>Voice:</strong> polite, precise, slightly too close. Asks questions that each have exactly one answer. Measures doorways with his chain while talking.</p><h3>Sample dialogue</h3><ul><li>[COMMON] \"Good evening. Which door did you come in by? There is only one correct answer.\"</li><li>[COMMON] \"I don't arrest anyone. I close doors. It's usually enough.\"</li><li>[ASK] \"A sealed door that opens is a lie with hinges.\"</li><li>[ASK] \"Forty-one openings. One minute each. Same hour. That is not a draft.\"</li><li>[EARN] <em>(after the audit, talked to a delay)</em> \"One more minute, then it's closed, and it's in my book that I waited.\"</li><li>[EARN] <em>(lawful permit)</em> \"If the three records agree, then what passes is a lawful transfer, and it's my job to let it. I hate that you've made this my job.\"</li><li><em>(lied to)</em> \"Thank you. I'll be posting at noon regardless.\"</li><li><em>(to Lil)</em> \"And which door did you come in by?\" <em>(Lil: \"The front one. It was the front when I came in.\")</em></li></ul>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
          "page": "",
          "license": "",
          "rules": "2014",
          "revision": 1
        },
