    {
      "_id": "e932b5c54a4f070e",
      "name": "Side Quest: Forty-One Minutes",
      "type": "feat",
      "img": "icons/sundries/documents/document-sealed-red-yellow.webp",
      "system": {
        "description": {
          "value": "<h2>Side Quest: Forty-One Minutes (Part 7, Scene 5)</h2><p><strong>Hook:</strong> <em>\"Tomorrow at noon I post a notice and the door is sealed properly.\"</em> Delay him, persuade him, or outrun him. <strong>Never violence.</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Talk him down to a delay:</strong> Persuasion <strong>DC 15</strong> (advantage if T5's audit is done). He files <em>after</em> one more opening.</li><li><strong>Lawful permit:</strong> Persuasion <strong>DC 17</strong> with the audit done, or Pringus speaks for the records. A one-time irregular-transfer permit; makes the later return fully legal.</li><li><strong>Lie:</strong> Deception <strong>DC 16</strong>. He goes away, but the notice still posts at noon.</li><li><strong>Nan helps:</strong> whatever they choose, she can hold the tenth-hour trolley a few minutes so he is late to the cold door.</li></ul><p><strong>The clock:</strong> each night the party delays, he gets one step further (day 1 questions, day 2 Sabeline's contract under review, day 3 the notice posts regardless).</p>",
          "chat": ""
        },
        "source": {
          "custom": "Varrenmoor DM Guide, Part 7 (Session 14)",
          "book": "",
